Your project uses **MSTest v2 (2.2.10)** targeting `net6.0`. Here are the breaking changes that affect your code:

---

### 1. Assertion overloads removed
MSTest v3 removed `Assert.AreEqual(object, object)` and `Assert.AreSame(object, object)`. You need explicit generic types:

```csharp
// Line 13 — before
Assert.AreEqual(expected, actual);
// after
Assert.AreEqual<object>(expected, actual);

// Line 20 — before
Assert.AreSame(obj, obj);
// after
Assert.AreSame<object>(obj, obj);
```

### 2. DataRow strict type matching
On lines 24–25, `1L`/`2L` are `long` but the parameter `id` is `int`. v3 requires exact type match:

```csharp
// before
[DataRow(1L, "Alice")]
[DataRow(2L, "Bob")]
public void GetUserName_ReturnsCorrectName(int id, string expectedName)

// fix option A — change literals to int:
[DataRow(1, "Alice")]
[DataRow(2, "Bob")]

// fix option B — change parameter to long:
public void GetUserName_ReturnsCorrectName(long id, string expectedName)
```

### 3. Timeout behavior unified
Line 32's `[Timeout(3000)]` will still work, but behavior is now consistent across .NET Core and Framework. Verify the 3-second timeout is still appropriate.

### 4. Package update
Replace the three package references with the unified `MSTest` metapackage:

```xml
<!-- Remove these -->
<PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestFramework" Version="2.2.10" />
<PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestAdapter" Version="2.2.10" />
<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.5.0" />

<!-- Add this -->
<PackageReference Include="MSTest" Version="3.8.0" />
```

### 5. Target framework
`net6.0` is supported by MSTest v3 — no change needed. (Consider upgrading to `net8.0` LTS separately since .NET 6 is end-of-life.)

